# User guide and module manual (mandatory on feature work)

Whenever you **introduce, change, or remove** anything that affects **what users see or do** in the Web Portal (screens, flows, labels, routes, permissions, navigation), you **must update documentation in the same change** before that work is considered complete or committed.

## What to update

1. **In-app user guide** (new tab + full guide): `WebPortal/help/index.html`, and when layout/behaviour of the help UI itself changes: `WebPortal/help/help-shell.css`, `WebPortal/help/help-shell.js`, `WebPortal/help/assets/`. The **documentation hub** is `WebPortal/help/help-index.html` (links between guides and manual chapters); update its links when you add routes or major topics.
2. **Standalone overview doc** (`WebPortal/assets/docs/user-guide.html` + `user-guide.css`): public-style single-page guide (quick start, navigation, workflows, modules, roles, troubleshooting). Update it when you add or rename major sidebar areas, streams, or troubleshooting tips—keep it aligned with `user-manual.html` at a high level.
3. **Module manual** (printable / by-module reference): `WebPortal/help/user-manual.html` and `WebPortal/help/user-manual.css` — add or revise the chapter for the affected module, and if `WebPortal/js/appRouteConfig.json` changed, update the **Appendix — Route catalogue** in `user-manual.html` to match.
4. **Help links on screens**: run `node scripts/apply_user_guide_help_links.mjs` from the repo root after adding or renaming help anchors, so each screen keeps a `macavation-help-link` to `help/index.html#…`.
5. **Screenshots** (when the visible UI changed): `cd "Playwright Tests" && npm run capture-user-guide` per project convention.

From the Web Portal, **Help** (`macavation-help-link`) opens `help/index.html` in a **new browser tab** (not an in-app modal), with **one topic** when a hash is present plus a compact **SVG** where relevant; **Full user guide** / `?full=1` lists every section. Sticky **Documentation navigation** on help pages links back to **`help-index.html`**. The **User manual (by module)** is linked from the help intro (`user-manual.html`).

## Checklist for a new or changed feature

```
Feature name:         [e.g. Dashboard Widgets]
Anchor ID:            [e.g. dashboard-widgets]
App location:         [e.g. Home → Dashboard]
Summary:              [1–2 sentences on what the feature does and why]
Diagrams:             [flow diagram / screenshot callout / none]
Help button location: [file path, e.g. modules/dashboard/html/dashboard.html]
```

Add a section in `WebPortal/help/index.html` with matching `id` (and generator/script workflow your team uses), add the **Help** link on the screen, and update **`user-manual.html`** and the **`assets/docs`** overview (`user-guide.html`) if the module’s purpose, navigation, or high-level workflow changed.

## Do not commit

- `Playwright Tests/test-results/` or any file inside it (local artifacts only).
